      {
        "id": "E2",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Tackling GPU Bottlenecks in Plane-Wave DFT with K-Point Batching and Mixed Precision",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/tackling-gpu-bottlenecks-in-plane-wave-dft-with-k-point-batching-and-mixed-precision/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-18T15:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-20T18:35:01.681Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E3",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Daviator, a new NVIDIA library of GPU kernels, replaces sequential k-point processing in VASP with batched GPU operations including a batched Davidson eigensolver, eliminating the small-system GPU performance bottleneck in plane-wave DFT.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/tackling-gpu-bottlenecks-in-plane-wave-dft-with-k-point-batching-and-mixed-precision/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-18T15:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-20T18:35:01.681Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E4",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "A mixed precision execution layer leverages FP32 arithmetic and storage for selected Davidson solver components while keeping numerically sensitive steps in FP64, delivering roughly 2x end-to-end acceleration on GPUs with high FP32:FP64 ratios such as the RTX PRO 6000.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/tackling-gpu-bottlenecks-in-plane-wave-dft-with-k-point-batching-and-mixed-precision/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-18T15:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-20T18:35:01.681Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E5",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "The mixed precision workflow uses configurable floating-point types to identify minimum required precision per kernel, enabling targeted FP32 adoption with FP64 islands for convergence-critical operations.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/tackling-gpu-bottlenecks-in-plane-wave-dft-with-k-point-batching-and-mixed-precision/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-18T15:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-20T18:35:01.681Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Daviator and its mixed precision option are available through the NVIDIA ALCHEMI VASP microservice by setting LDAVIATOR=True and LDAVIATOR_MIXED_PRECISION=1 in the INCAR file, with existing VASP inputs working without modification.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/tackling-gpu-bottlenecks-in-plane-wave-dft-with-k-point-batching-and-mixed-precision/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-18T15:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-20T18:35:01.681Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "The second, a new mixed precision execution layer, enables further performance gains, especially on inference-class GPUs with a high FP32:FP64 throughput ratio.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/tackling-gpu-bottlenecks-in-plane-wave-dft-with-k-point-batching-and-mixed-precision/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-18T15:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-20T18:35:01.681Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "For large systems, the work per k-point can fully saturate a GPU, but for small systems with dense k-point grids, the hundreds of small GPU dispatches per step causes kernel launch overhead to dominate compute time.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/tackling-gpu-bottlenecks-in-plane-wave-dft-with-k-point-batching-and-mixed-precision/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-18T15:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-20T18:35:01.681Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E9",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Additionally, plane-wave DFT traditionally runs in FP64, a conservative default that guarantees accuracy throughout the solver pipeline.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/tackling-gpu-bottlenecks-in-plane-wave-dft-with-k-point-batching-and-mixed-precision/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-18T15:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-20T18:35:01.681Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E10",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Daviator’s mixed precision can be enabled by setting LDAVIATOR_MIXED_PRECISION to 1 (0 is FP64).",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/tackling-gpu-bottlenecks-in-plane-wave-dft-with-k-point-batching-and-mixed-precision/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-18T15:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-20T18:35:01.681Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E11",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "The following INCAR parameters are available to configure the use of mixed precision specifically for Daviator (Table 1).",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/tackling-gpu-bottlenecks-in-plane-wave-dft-with-k-point-batching-and-mixed-precision/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-18T15:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-20T18:35:01.681Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E12",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "True = FP32 Enable/Disable Mixed Precision (FP32 = mixed arithmetic and FP32 storage in Daviator)",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/tackling-gpu-bottlenecks-in-plane-wave-dft-with-k-point-batching-and-mixed-precision/",
